From 3bec1f1bc26f7d712ebdeaf3b9a8fa23dbdc6b3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:00:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] render passes: show the real frame and lock presents to
 VBlanks

Three presentation fixes for render-pass frame interpolation, found on
Action Man: Mission Xtreme (PAL, 25 fps game, Frame Rate mod):

- A schedule deadline ends the output period it fills, but
  pass_gen_present read it as that period's start. At 50 FPS the
  presents fell at phases 0.5 and 1.0, so the in-between was shown
  twice and the real frame never; at 100 the real frame was up for
  ~5 ms of 40. Read each deadline as the start of its period, and plan
  pass phases on the same origin.
- At output rates that are a whole multiple of the VBlank rate (50, 100
  on PAL) take the generation phase from the VBlank count and re-lock
  the output grid to each source interval. When a heavy scene ran the
  guest at 0.98x, the free-running clock slid against the VBlanks: two
  presents landed in one VBlank and none in the next, scrambling the
  order for seconds at a time.
- Allow 50 FPS interpolation (one in-between per 25 fps PAL frame).

Also: PSXDrawReplay::max_move (per-title cut limit), and diagnostics
for debug builds: PSX_RENDER_PASS_ALPHA (force a pass phase),
psx_projection_replay_kept_total(), PSX_PRESENT_LOG (one line per
swap), and render_pass_dump file names carrying the generation order
and period.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QwPTgFkfWXATrAfYHXR5kA
